WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.083
RYAN MATSUMOTO: Today,
we're talking about updates

00:00:02.083 --> 00:00:04.140
to infrastructure,
Memorystore, Looker,

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:05.880
and contextual tutorials.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.280
I'm Ryan, and welcome
to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.830
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:12.340
In the span of
just three months,

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.100
Google Cloud teams
delivered a ton

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.810
of new and innovative
capabilities

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:18.690
for compute, networking,
storage, serverless,

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:19.920
and containers.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.010
From Transfer Appliance
to Tau VMs to scaling,

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:25.980
check out the summary to see
what you may have missed.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:28.440
Maintenance is critical,
but related downtimes

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:29.550
can be costly.

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.800
We're excited to announce
that Cloud Memorystore now

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.200
enables you to have more
control over when your Cloud

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:37.680
Memorystore for Redis instances
undergo routine maintenance.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.590
This control comes in the form
of rescheduling and advance

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:43.680
notification capabilities,
which will be familiar controls

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.270
for Cloud SQL users.

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:48.140
Head to the blog to learn more.

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:50.660
The Extension Framework is
a fully hosted development

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:52.610
platform that enables
developers to build

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:54.860
any data-powered
application, workflow,

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:56.840
or tool right in Looker.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:59.730
By eliminating the need to spin
up and host infrastructure,

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:01.610
the Extension Framework
lets developers

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:05.445
focus on building great
experiences for their users.

00:01:05.445 --> 00:01:07.070
Do you know that
there's a way to learn

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:08.903
how to use Google Cloud
products built right

00:01:08.903 --> 00:01:10.580
into the Google Cloud console?

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:13.730
In-console tutorials can walk
you through complete actions

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:16.640
without having to open another
window for documentation.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.400
Features like spotlights,
buttons, and code snippets

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:22.400
make getting your project up
and running easier than ever.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.560
They'll pop up automatically,
but to check out

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.810
our list of existing
Firestore tutorials,

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:28.987
head to the linked blog.

00:01:28.987 --> 00:01:31.070
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:33.570
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:34.850
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:36.690
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:39.130
We'll see you in the Cloud.

